    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0346" n="334" xml:id="pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr.,
                        to the Chinese Minister of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Chen
                    Cheng</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-15">April 15, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Control Group here in Chungking is nearing completion of its detailed
                    planning and will soon move to Peiping to join Executive Headquarters.</p>
                <p>It is General Marshall’s desire that this Group proceed to Peiping completely
                    organized. It is therefore requested that you designate by name the three or
                    four officers you wish to serve with the Control Group and inform this
                    office.</p>
                <p>A similar memorandum has been sent to General Chou En-lai.<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d113-f1"/></p>
                <closer>For <signed> Lieutenant General Gillem: <lb/> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Hart Caughey</hi>
                    </signed><lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. C.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
